nit`, and a normal page navigation doesn't send the `Authorization` header. The token only goes out with `fetch` requests from the SPA. Now that endpoint is a POST that returns `{authorize_url}`, and the button calls it through `api()` and then does `window.location.assign(...)` (`server.py`, `static/app.js`).\n2. **Intervals answered 400 `invalid_request` even for a manually pasted link.** The scope list had `ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE` and `CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`, and Intervals rejects repeated scopes. I changed it to `ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE` in `config.py`. This is an inference: the response body is a generic `invalid_request`, not \"Duplicate scope\". But the error started after calendar sync was added, and when Rivera connected the scope had no repeats.\n3. **Rivera was asked to reconnect after an hour.** Intervals tokens have no expiry and no `refresh_token`, but the code set a made-up 1-hour lifetime. A background thread then wiped the working token. I removed the fake lifetime and the refresh thread. Now the token is dropped only when Intervals returns a 401, and the user sees `revoked, reconnect`.\n\n**Mock test:** a GET to the init endpoint now gets 404, and a POST without a token gets 401. Through the full flow, the callback redirects back as connected and wellness data comes through. After a simulated revocation, the user gets \"reconnect\" instead of an error.\n\n**Things to know:**\n- Rivera's token, and anyone else's already marked `expired, reconnect`, was erased in the database, so they'll need to reconnect once. The button works now.\n- Ports 8766 and 8799 already had someone else's `server.py` processes (PIDs 88628/88629, started at 23:49). I didn't touch them and tested on other ports. If that's an old dev server, restart it or it won't pick up the fixes.\n\n**From your colleague's note**, these parts helped: init as a POST (cause 1), the duplicate-scope rule (cause 2), and no refresh token with handling revocation on the first 401 (cause 3). I didn't use these:\n- **Only three fields in the token exchange:** our request also sends `grant_type` and `redirect_uri`, but Rivera's exchange worked with them, so I left it.\n- **`SETTINGS:WRITE`:** we don't need that scope.\n- **JWT `state`, the account-mismatch check on reconnect, and token encryption:** worth adding later as a separate task, but they don't explain these failures.","ttft_ms":1646,"type":"result","duration_ms":99125,"uuid":"10d9ac45-7bc9-4b3a-949f-e80de7266b41","ttft_stream_ms":885,"time_to_request_ms":36,"first_content_frame_ms":885,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":18,"outputTokens":10461,"cacheReadInputTokens":286084,"cacheCreationInputTokens":26907,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.4817648,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1434,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
